  "body": "@domenic mentioned in #500 that\r\n\r\n> Sequences of percent-encoded bytes, string percent decoded, should not cause UTF-8 decode without BOM or fail to return failure.\r\n\r\nIs confusing. What it is mainly trying to say is that, e.g., \"`%FF`\"  should not be used as 0xFF would end up as U+FFFD when UTF-8 decoded (or return failure for the above cited algorithm). There might be edge cases however where encoding non-string data in URLs is fine.\r\n\r\nBut perhaps we should simply stay out of this?",
